# Match WLANPi OS, which is what WLAN Commander is actually written against.
#
# Measured on a WLANPi Go running WLANPi OS 25.10.2:
#     wlanpi ALL=(ALL:ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
# That is why WC's SSH layer has no sudo-password mechanism outside the Passpoint
# path -- every other command assumes `sudo -n` just works, and `sudo -n` fails
# immediately rather than prompting when it does not.
#
# Upstream scopes this to iw/ip/tcpdump/dumpcap, which covers scan and capture but
# not the interface-busy recovery path (`sudo pgrep -f <pat>` then kill), nor
# `systemctl stop` for releasing a radio. Enumerating the shortfall was tried and
# rejected: the list came from grepping command templates, which demonstrably
# misses cases, and it would silently break the next time WC reached for a binary
# nobody predicted. A whitelist that has to stay in sync with another repo's
# internals is not a boundary, it is a latent bug.
#
# The trade-off is real and deliberate: combined with the published default
# password this grants root to anyone who can reach SSH. That is precisely the
# WLANPi posture on the same lab networks, and these are survey sensors, not
# multi-user hosts. Change the `pi` password before putting one anywhere less
# trusted -- the upstream README says the same thing about the password alone.
pi ALL=(ALL:ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
